### 4. Git push commands
To push to GitHub and trigger the workflow:

```bash
# Add the remote (replace with your actual repo URL)
git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/my_website.git

# Push to main branch (triggers the GitHub Actions workflow)
git push -u origin main

# The workflow will then build and deploy to gh-pages
```

To run the workflow manually (after pushing): go to the repo's **Actions** tab → select "Deploy Site" → **Run workflow**.

